[h1]Flavorium Universalis - Rhomania v0.4.1: The Settlement of the West[/h1]

[i]Compatible with EU5 1.4.* | Requires: Flavorium Universalis and the Fate of the Phoenix content pack[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]The West no longer ends early[/h2]

The West situation began one step from the Reabsorption ending, and a single loyal prefecture could reach it within a decade, ending the situation with almost nothing of the west recovered and no warning. The four endings now take time to reach and come with a decision.

[list]
[*] [b]Locked at first:[/b] no ending can be reached until the West has run fifty years with at least two prefectures seated. The counters still move in that time, and the panel shows how far along it is.
[*] [b]Five years in a corner:[/b] once the endings are open, the counters must stay in a corner for five years to settle it. Entering one fires [b]The West Is Settling[/b], which lets you steer both counters back toward the middle for 150 gold and 20 political influence. Leaving the corner resets the count, and the panel shows the year reached.
[*] [b]The settlement:[/b] at the end of the five years, a final event lets you choose the form of the ending. Reabsorption can bring Writs of Reunion (cheaper annexation of the old prefectures) or keep the exarchs on as governors. The diarchy can crown a Caesar of the West or keep him a colleague in name. An acclamation can be accepted or refused, and neglect ended quietly or with a last inspection.
[*] The Age of Revolutions deadline is unchanged.
[*] [b]Existing saves:[/b] a West already under way starts its fifty years from the moment the save is loaded.
[/list]

[h2]Localization[/h2]

French, German and Spanish are updated for the new events and panel text.
